---
/**
 * GRPO's inverted U: the reward that matters peaks and comes back down while the collapse keeps
 * climbing.
 *
 * Three runs of 400 steps from the same checkpoint with the same seed, and nothing changing but
 * the learning rate. Two series, both measured on 300 held-out positions, each on its own axis.
 *
 * The solid line (left axis) is the reward with `cp_best` taken from the **engine's own best
 * move** -- the one that cannot be raised by making the policy more deterministic. It rises,
 * peaks at 5e-6, and falls back at 2e-5. It is drawn as points joined by a line rather than bars,
 * because the axis does not start at zero: a bar on a truncated axis lies about proportions, a
 * point on a ticked axis does not.
 *
 * The dashed line (right axis, "grupos planos") is the share of validation groups whose eight
 * candidates were all the same move. It climbs monotonically: 0.370, 0.453, 0.490. So the fall in
 * the reward is not noise, it has a mechanism sitting right next to it -- the policy is buying
 * reward with determinism, and past a point the purchase stops paying.
 *
 * The leftmost run is the one that got published: it is the only one where the collapse indicator
 * goes *down* (from 0.387 before training) while the reward goes up.
 */
interface Run {
  lr: string;
  absolute: number;
  group: number;
  flat: number;
}

const BEFORE = { absolute: 0.8325, flat: 0.387 };

const runs: Run[] = [
  { lr: '1e-6', absolute: 0.8413, group: 0.8741, flat: 0.37 },
  { lr: '5e-6', absolute: 0.8592, group: 0.8928, flat: 0.453 },
  { lr: '2e-5', absolute: 0.8402, group: 0.8929, flat: 0.49 },
];

// Plot area.
const LEFT = 150;
const RIGHT = 590;
const TOP_Y = 44;
const BOTTOM_Y = 180;

// Left axis: reward against the engine's best move.
const R_LOW = 0.83;
const R_HIGH = 0.87;
const rewardTicks = [0.83, 0.85, 0.87];
const rewardY = (value: number) =>
  BOTTOM_Y - ((value - R_LOW) / (R_HIGH - R_LOW)) * (BOTTOM_Y - TOP_Y);

// Right axis: share of flat validation groups.
const F_LOW = 0.35;
const F_HIGH = 0.51;
const flatTicks = [0.35, 0.43, 0.51];
const flatY = (share: number) =>
  BOTTOM_Y - ((share - F_LOW) / (F_HIGH - F_LOW)) * (BOTTOM_Y - TOP_Y);

const x = (index: number) => LEFT + 30 + index * 190;

const rewardPoints = runs.map((run, index) => `${x(index)},${rewardY(run.absolute)}`).join(' ');
const flatPoints = runs.map((run, index) => `${x(index)},${flatY(run.flat)}`).join(' ');

const es = (value: number, digits: number) => value.toFixed(digits).replace('.', ',');
---

<figure class="fig fig--overopt" tabindex="0">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 640 250"
    role="img"
    aria-label="Tres corridas de GRPO que solo se diferencian en la tasa de aprendizaje, con dos series sobre dos ejes. La línea continua, en el eje izquierdo, es la recompensa medida contra el mejor movimiento disponible: 0,8413 con tasa 1e-6, sube a 0,8592 con 5e-6 y vuelve a bajar a 0,8402 con 2e-5. La línea a trazos, en el eje derecho rotulado grupos planos, es la proporción de grupos de validación donde las ocho candidatas eran la misma jugada: 0,370, luego 0,453, luego 0,490, subiendo siempre. La ganancia se dobla y cae mientras el colapso sigue creciendo."
  >
    <g font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--muted)">
      <line
        x1={LEFT}
        y1={TOP_Y}
        x2={LEFT}
        y2={BOTTOM_Y}
        stroke="var(--line)"
        stroke-width="0.8"
      ></line>
      <line
        x1={RIGHT}
        y1={TOP_Y}
        x2={RIGHT}
        y2={BOTTOM_Y}
        stroke="var(--line)"
        stroke-width="0.8"
      ></line>
      <line
        x1={LEFT}
        y1={BOTTOM_Y}
        x2={RIGHT}
        y2={BOTTOM_Y}
        stroke="var(--line)"
        stroke-width="0.8"
      ></line>

      {rewardTicks.map((tick) => (
        <g>
          <line
            x1={LEFT - 4}
            y1={rewardY(tick)}
            x2={LEFT}
            y2={rewardY(tick)}
            stroke="var(--line)"
            stroke-width="0.8"
          />
          <text
            x={LEFT - 8}
            y={rewardY(tick) + 3}
            text-anchor="end"
            font-size="9"
            fill="var(--accent-text-aa)"
          >
            {es(tick, 2)}
          </text>
        </g>
      ))}
      <text
        x={LEFT - 8}
        y={TOP_Y - 14}
        text-anchor="end"
        font-size="9"
        fill="var(--accent-text-aa)"
      >
        recompensa contra el motor
      </text>

      {flatTicks.map((tick) => (
        <g>
          <line
            x1={RIGHT}
            y1={flatY(tick)}
            x2={RIGHT + 4}
            y2={flatY(tick)}
            stroke="var(--line)"
            stroke-width="0.8"
          />
          <text x={RIGHT + 8} y={flatY(tick) + 3} font-size="9" fill="var(--ink)">
            {es(tick, 2)}
          </text>
        </g>
      ))}
      <text x={RIGHT + 40} y={TOP_Y - 14} font-size="9" fill="var(--ink)" text-anchor="end">
        grupos planos
      </text>

      <line
        x1={LEFT}
        y1={rewardY(BEFORE.absolute)}
        x2={RIGHT}
        y2={rewardY(BEFORE.absolute)}
        stroke="var(--accent)"
        stroke-width="0.7"
        stroke-dasharray="4 3"
        stroke-opacity="0.6"
      ></line>
      <text
        x={LEFT + 6}
        y={rewardY(BEFORE.absolute) - 4}
        font-size="8"
        fill="var(--accent-text-aa)"
      >
        antes de entrenar: {es(BEFORE.absolute, 4)}
      </text>

      <polyline
        points={rewardPoints}
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--accent)"
        stroke-width="1.6"
      ></polyline>
      <polyline
        points={flatPoints}
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--ink)"
        stroke-width="1.2"
        stroke-dasharray="3 2"
      ></polyline>

      {runs.map((run, index) => (
        <g>
          <circle
            cx={x(index)}
            cy={rewardY(run.absolute)}
            r="4"
            fill="var(--accent)"
            stroke="var(--frame-bg, #fff)"
            stroke-width="1"
          />
          <text
            x={x(index)}
            y={rewardY(run.absolute) - 9}
            text-anchor="middle"
            font-size="9"
            fill="var(--accent-text-aa)"
          >
            {es(run.absolute, 4)}
          </text>
          <circle
            cx={x(index)}
            cy={flatY(run.flat)}
            r="3.5"
            fill="var(--frame-bg, #fff)"
            stroke="var(--ink)"
            stroke-width="1.3"
          />
          <text
            x={x(index)}
            y={flatY(run.flat) + 15}
            text-anchor="middle"
            font-size="9"
            fill="var(--ink)"
          >
            {es(run.flat, 3)}
          </text>
          <text
            x={x(index)}
            y={BOTTOM_Y + 16}
            text-anchor="middle"
            font-size="10"
            fill="var(--ink)"
          >
            lr {run.lr}
          </text>
        </g>
      ))}

      <text x={LEFT - 100} y="222" font-size="9">
        línea continua · recompensa contra el motor (eje izquierdo): se dobla y cae
      </text>
      <text x={LEFT - 100} y="238" font-size="9">
        línea a trazos · grupos planos (eje derecho): sube en las tres; antes de entrenar, 0,387
      </text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="caption">
    La recompensa que no se puede falsear sube, se dobla y baja. El indicador de colapso sube en las
    tres. La forma de la curva es lo que distingue mejorar de sobreoptimizar.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
